# Gap analysis — spec 0038 "UI standardization"

*This is the gap-analysis companion to `.summary-md` (the narrative) and `.stat-md`
(the numbers) — not a substitute for either. It tracks what was asked for versus what
was authored, and what was authored versus what shipped.*

**Preliminary spec — discovered by inference.** The `.history` first spec-input row
(`actor: user`, `intent: spec`) reads: *"Read the preliminary spec:
`…\.manual\006-ui-standardization-preliminary-spec.md` and write a full spec."* So the
preliminary is `.manual/006-ui-standardization-preliminary-spec.md`, and both gap
passes below run.

**Basis of the spec→implementation pass.** This pass reads the arc records — the 47/47
committed green slices (each through all five gates plus a code-judge review), the
contract-commit log, and the authored `.spec-md`/`.spec-jsonl`. It is **not** a
line-by-line code audit; items that would need one to confirm are marked
`unverified`.

