| spec→impl | unverified | whole arc | Coverage of the per-Part acceptance criteria is inferred from 47/47 green slices + committed contracts, not independently re-derived from the code here. |

One gap was **found and closed inside the arc**, so it is not residual: at slice 032
the code-judge caught the Part K per-series show/hide chart toggle
(`ToggleSeriesVisibility` / `applyHidden`) shipping with zero test coverage; the
resolver's hint added the round-trip test and the slice closed green before commit.

## Verdict

High completeness with no residual gaps of consequence. Every one of the preliminary's
14 phases entered the authored spec unchanged, and all 47 authored slices shipped green
across all five gates and code-judge review. The only "gaps" are the spec's own,
pre-agreed out-of-scope deferrals — the ConstantMueller editor, the `.ocproj` disk
format, the real inverse solver, app-level DB coupling, and export — none of which was
expected to ship this cycle. The single mid-arc coverage gap (the chart toggle) was
caught by review and closed before commit. The one caveat worth stating plainly: this
spec→implementation pass trusts the arc's green record rather than an independent code
audit, so a reader wanting per-Part acceptance confirmation should still spot-check the
landed code for the parts they care about.
